## Top 3 must-fix

1. **Tailwind's `dark:` variant is bound to the OS media query, not the site's `.dark` class.** No `@custom-variant dark` exists anywhere; the built CSS puts all `dark:` utilities inside one `@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark)` block. Same element, site theme dark both times: OS-light → `bg-blue-50` (near-white), OS-dark → `dark:bg-blue-950/30`. 370 `dark:` utilities are affected; six Callouts on this essay render light-grey text on a white panel. One line fixes it.
2. **`--accent` never paints.** `global.css:116/:170` set the real violet, then `:1770/:1792` (leftover shadcn) override it with bare HSL triples at equal specificity. Measured on `.reading-companion__header`: token = `217.2 32.6% 17.5%`, computed colour = `--text-primary`. 19 live elements plus the reading-progress bar, which paints nothing.
3. **`ReadingCompanion` never sticks.** `xl:self-start` (`PostLayout.astro:211`) caps the grid item at content height, so the sticky child has no travel. Measured: rect top 457 → −402 across 859px of scroll (1:1, no pinning), off-screen by `scrollY ≈ 2462` while the article is 23306px tall. Violates V5 and §7 item 3 directly.

A4 (Evidence Focus unreachable — 0 evidence links outside `<template>`, verified statically and in the live DOM) is close behind and arguably the worst *functional* gap.

## What I could not verify

No-JS behaviour, keyboard focus containment/restoration, and the two distinct return semantics — all read in source but not driven, so they are listed unverified rather than passed. Tier A 03's split composition and Tier A 07's managed-variation comparison had nothing rendered to photograph. Section E of the report lists these plus four smaller gaps.

Two scope corrections worth your attention: the mobile Contents sheet and the unwired `PullQuote`/`ContextualNote`/`ReceiptDisclosure` are **P0-D and V12 work per DIRECTION.md**, not P0-B/C defects, so I put them in a separate section rather than the must-fix list. The dark nav-in-light-theme and the React #418 error reproduce on other essays and are pre-existing site-wide. I also corrected my own draft mid-way: I initially read thread/evidence overlays as unwired, but `focus-host.ts` intercepts by pathname, so they work — and A1 meant my first dark screenshots were unfair, which is why I re-captured.
